@@ -82,6 +82,27 @@ platforms and later actors still run afterwards. Reference ownership and public
 arbitrary-callback dispatch retain the unskipped walk: this proof does not
 permit suppressing arbitrary callbacks or newly added box event behavior.
 
+## Prepared terrain registration spans
+
+The native instance table uses `RunnerRunMembership` for registration, retaining
+the scalar table under the existing scalar-ownership reference selector.
+Consecutive fresh terrain slots with the same object and consecutive lifetime
+IDs share a descriptor; the locator is not another identity/order list.
+Removal and re-registration split runs as needed. Descriptor capacity still
+permits every slot to become a singleton. The maintained actor/thin-platform
+projection preserves registration order without visiting ordinary walls.
+
+Only the existing callback-free prepared terrain segment may defer registration
+publication. Each birth still allocates its original shared chronology stamp
+and performs spatial and layer work. Registration spans flush at an object,
+slot or lifetime discontinuity and at segment end, including a failed prefix.
+The certified Create path reads the prepared tile plan and publishes dirty
+queues; it cannot query registrations or invoke a game callback. Event-bearing
+or observed Creates continue through scalar immediate publication. Adding such
+an observer to the prepared path requires flushing before it, not exposing a
+partially published registry. Layer ownership, inactive cutoffs and activation
+reconciliation remain independent of this registration representation.
+
 ## Immutable room index publication
 
 `AmigaRoomTerrainPlan` accelerates only the serialized main-room placements.
